ORDINANCE NO. ________

ENTITLED: "AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CERTAIN SECTIONS OF CHAPTER 44,
SOLID WASTE, AND CHAPTER 56, NOISE CONTROL, OF TITLE 8,
HEALTH AND SAFETY, AND FURTHER AMENDING CERTAIN
SECTIONS OF CHAPTER 8, OFFENSES AGAINST PUBLIC PEACE AND
DECENCY, AND CHAPTER 12, OFFENSES AGAINST PROPERTY, OF
TITLE 9, PUBLIC PEACE AND WELFARE, OF THE MUNICIPAL CODE
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, TO ELIMINATE THE
POTENTIAL IMPOSITION OF A JAIL SENTENCE FOR VIOLATION OF
SPECIFIED CODE PROVISIONS."

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:

Section 1.  That Section 8.44.010, Purpose—Authority—General provisions, and Section
8.44.030, General Regulations, of Chapter 8.44, Solid Waste, and Section 8.56.010, Prohibited
When Excessive, of Chapter 8.56, Noise Control, of Title 8, Health and Safety, of the City of
Cheyenne, Wyoming, are hereby amended as set out in this section:

8.44.010 - Purpose; —Authority—General provisions.authority; general provisions.

A. The purpose of this chapter is to protect public health, safety, and welfare by regulating the
accumulation, storage, transportation, and disposal of solid waste or refuse to prevent fire,
health or other safety hazards, to eliminate undesirable pests, and to promote the aesthetic
appearance of the community.

B. Authority is granted cities and towns in Wyo. Stat. Sections W.S. 15-1-103(a)(xxi) and
(a)(xli) to adopt ordinances, resolutions and regulations necessary for health, safety and
welfare and to "purchase, lease or rent land within or without the corporate limits for the
deposit of refuse matter, govern the use of the land and make reasonable rules and
requirements for hauling refuse."

C. All solid waste accumulated in the city must be collected, conveyed and disposed of by the
city under the supervision of the director of the public works director, department or
designated representative. his or her designee.

1. The public works director is authorized to create promulgate rules and regulations
pertaining to solid waste collection, conveyance, and disposal pursuant to in accordance
with the Wyoming Administrative Procedure Act. The public works director will shall
present the fee schedule to the city council for approval.

2. Except as provided in Section 8.44.030(E)(6), 8.44.030(G)(7) of this chapter and as
further provided in this paragraph, all solid waste accumulated in the city shall be
collected, conveyed, and disposed of by the city. No person, other than persons duly
authorized by the city, may collect, convey over any of the streets or alleys of the city,
11:26 am, Feb 07, 2024
