Chapter 8.56 – NOISE CONTROL

8.56.010 – Prohibited when excessive;. penalty.

A. The making and creating of an No person shall make or otherwise create excessive or
unusually loud noise within the city as heard without measurement or heard and measured
in a manner prescribed herein, is hereby declared to be unlawful; as provided by Section
8.56.040 of this chapter, except when made under and in compliance with a permit issued
pursuant to under Section 8.56.060 of this chapter.

B. Any person who violates subsection (A) of this section is guilty of a misdemeanor
punishable by a fine of not more than seven hundred fifty dollars ($750.00).

