1. Discharge any gun, pistol, revolver or any firearm, of any description, or explode or set
off any squib, firecracker, or other things thing containing powder or other combustible
material or make any other improper noise calculated intended to disturb the peace of
anyone in the area;

2. Operate any vehicle, machinery, or other equipment, or vehicle which that emits loud
noise and thereby disturbs the peace and tranquility of any person;

3. Be As the owner of, or possessor of, a dog, which barks allow the dog to bark
excessively and disturbs disturb the peace and tranquility of any person; in the area;

4. Cause, provoke or engage in any fight, brawl or riotous conduct so as to that endanger
endangers the life, limb, health or property of another person;

5. Commit an act in a violent or tumultuous manner toward another person whereby where
that the other person is placed in danger of his or her life, limb or health;

6. Use profane, obscene, or offensive or otherwise provocative language directed toward
another person, or others, and calculated which language is intended to provoke a
breach of the peace. For purposes of this section, the term "provocative language" shall
mean insulting words or fighting words" or those words by which their very utterance
inflict injury or tend to incite an immediate breach of the peace;

7. Perform any act or gesture of rude, improper or indecent behavior, directed at another
person and calculated intended to provoke a breach of the peace;

8. Incite or attempt to incite a riot. For purposes of this section, subsection, the term "riot"
shall mean a tumultuous disturbance of the peace by persons assembled and acting with
common intent to the terror of the people of the city, either in assemblage while
executing a lawful enterprise in a violent or turbulent manner or in assemblage while
executing an unlawful enterprise in a violent or turbulent manner; or

9. Urinate in any public way or place which that is public in nature or any place open to
the public view.

B. No person shall cause, or be instrumental in causing, any disturbance of property in the
city. Any person or assemblage of persons shall be deemed guilty of disturbance of
property if they: shall:

1. Throw any stone or other missile at any person, animal, vehicle, building or other
private or public property;

2. Take and carry away the personal goods of another person or public property without
consent of the owner or lawful possessor;

3. Enter or remain upon another's property without consent of the owner or possessor; or
