9.12.060 – Shoplifting;. penalty.

A. Shoplifting is prohibited and declared to be unlawful. Any person who wilfully conceals
No person shall willfully conceal or wilfully takes take possession of any goods good
offered for sale by a wholesaler or retail store or other mercantile establishment, without
the knowledge or consent of the owner thereof and with intent to convert the goods good
to his or her own use without paying the purchase price. thereof, is shoplifting. The
following acts or deceptive conduct shall constitute prima facie evidence of concealing:

1.
Hiding any good upon the person, or in a container, or otherwise removing such
merchandise from full view while upon the premises;

2.
Removing, changing or altering any price tag affixed to any good;

3.
Transferring or moving any good upon the premises to obtain a lower price than
the merchandise was offered for sale by the merchant; or

4.
Abandoning or disposing of any good in such a manner that the merchant will be
deprived of all or part of the value of the good.

For purposes of this section, the term "conceals" shall mean any act of deception done wilfully
or knowingly upon or outside the premises of a wholesale or retail store or other mercantile
establishment with the intent to deprive the owner therein of all or part of the value of the
merchandise. The following acts or deceptive conduct are prima facie evidence of concealing:

A. Concealing merchandise upon the person, or in a container, or otherwise removing such
merchandise from full view while upon the premises;

B. Removing, changing, or altering any price tag;

C. Transferring or moving any merchandise upon the premises to obtain a lower price than
the merchandise was offered for sale by the merchant; or

D. Abandoning or disposing of any merchandise in such manner that the merchant will be
deprived of all or part of the value of the merchandise.

B. Any peace officer, merchant or merchant's employee who has reasonable cause for
believing to believe that a person has committed the offense of shoplifting as defined under
this section, may detain and interrogate such person in regard thereto in a reasonable
manner and for a reasonable time.
```

